# CodeQL false-positive baseline -- local ai-review / reviewdrain codeql-python path.
# Consumed by codeql-review --baseline (auto-attached when this file is present);
# format matches codeql-sarif-fingerprints.py / codeql-sarif-filter.py:
#   <ruleId>\t<repo-relative-path>\t<primaryLocationLineHash>:<version>
# Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored. Each entry is a reviewed false positive
# or by-design finding -- no real credential leak. Rationale (drift-proof):
#
# - torrc_gen.py gen_torrc() DEBUG prints log bridge_type (args[0]) and
#   custom_bridges (args[1]); the proxy password is args[6]. CodeQL container-taint
#   flags the whole args list and cannot distinguish the index, so these never emit
#   the password.
# - tor_status.py write_to_temp_then_move() prints content via redact_credentials(),
#   which masks every credential option (Socks5ProxyPassword, *ProxyAuthenticator,
#   HashedControlPassword, ...) to [REDACTED] before the print; CodeQL does not
#   recognize the sanitizer.
# - tor_status.py comm_file.write() stores the Tor config IPC file, which must carry
#   the plaintext proxy credential for Tor to use it; it cannot be masked. By design.
